# What not to upload when deploying from the CLI.
#
# public/EPI holds 3,868 files totalling 1.5GB, of which git tracks 494 (46MB).
# The rest is source and intermediate material from the ingest pipeline — the
# PDFs documents were converted from, the raw XML, and the page images pulled
# out of each PDF. `vercel deploy` uploads the working directory rather than the
# commit, so it tried to push all 1.5GB and failed with "Upload aborted".
#
# None of this has ever been deployed: it is untracked, so no git-triggered
# build has ever included it either. Excluding it here makes a CLI deploy match
# what the repository would produce, rather than changing what production serves.
#
# The consequence, which predates this file: the rendered DCP in /doc-viewer
# references 481 extracted images under DCPs/images, and those images are not in
# the repository, so they do not render in production. Committing them (222MB
# for Hornsby alone) or moving them to object storage is the fix; ignoring them
# here neither causes nor worsens it.

public/EPI/DCPs/images/
public/EPI/DCPs/pdf/
public/EPI/xml/

# Scratch and local-only material.
Notebooks/
*.ipynb
